lesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0143127535?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Thinking in Bets","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0735216371.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Thinking in Bets by Annie Duke","quip":"A decision-making book for keeping one spectacular result from rewriting what the odds meant beforehand.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0735216371?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://nclottery.com/NewsBlogDetails/2026/10/13/Pick-3-players-win-over-1dot7-million-on-0-0-0","sourceName":"Read the October 13 North Carolina Education Lottery report","sourcePublisher":"North Carolina Education Lottery","socialSummary":"The North Carolina Education Lottery said the October 12 Pick 3 evening result 0-0-0 paid 4,917 winning tickets a combined $1,762,353; the agency published the payout on October 13.","socialPunchline":"Blappos: The statewide terminal rebooted with the factory password and 4,917 people knew it."},
{"id":"oct13-perseverance-distance-record","isoDate":"2026-10-13","month":"October 2026","date":"Oct 13, 2026","place":"Jezero Crater, Mars","image":"assets/cards/oct13-perseverance-distance-record.webp","title":"A Robot Becomes the Off-World Mileage King","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/33096143","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"Reuters reported on October 13 that NASA's six-wheeled Perseverance rover had driven 28.1 miles (45.2 kilometers) on Mars, surpassing Opportunity's distance record for any vehicle on a world beyond Earth. NASA's own comparison marks the mileage as of October 11; Perseverance landed in Jezero Crater on February 18, 2021.","why":"This is a distance-and-durability record, not a speed record. A Jet Propulsion Laboratory project manager told Reuters that about 90% of Perseverance's drives are autonomous: the rover uses stereo images, a 3D terrain map and onboard path selection to travel safely between goals despite the communications delay between Earth and Mars.","angle":"Verified reporting ends above. The Blappos interpretation: the solar system's highest-mileage used car has one owner, 28.1 miles, extensive off-road use and absolutely no local pickup option. The magnet uses an original generic research rover and invented terrain—no NASA seal, JPL mark, mission photograph or claim that the record is finished growing.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"Mars Rover Curiosity: An Inside Account from Curiosity's Chief Engineer","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/1588344037.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Mars Rover Curiosity by Rob Manning and William L. Simon","quip":"An engineer's inside account of the rover lineage whose lessons helped make a 28.1-mile Martian road trip possible.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1588344037?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"The Design and Engineering of Curiosity","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/3319681443.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of The Design and Engineering of Curiosity by Emily Lakdawalla","quip":"A system-by-system guide to how a planetary rover sees, steers and works when roadside assistance is one planet away.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/3319681443?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Red Rover: Inside the Story of Robotic Space Exploration","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0465055982.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Red Rover by Roger Wiens","quip":"A human history of robotic planetary exploration for the very long relay race behind today's mileage crown.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0465055982?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://www.reuters.com/science/nasas-perseverance-rover-breaks-record-off-planet-driving-mars-2026-10-13/","sourceName":"Read the October 13 Reuters report","sourcePublisher":"Reuters","socialSummary":"Reuters reported that NASA's Perseverance rover reached 28.1 miles on Mars, passing Opportunity for the longest distance driven by any vehicle on another world; NASA dates the milestone mileage to October 11.","socialPunchline":"Blappos: One owner, 28.1 miles, extensive off-road use, local pickup unavailable."},
{"id":"oct12-zeekr-25cm-drift","isoDate":"2026-10-12","month":"October 2026","date":"Oct 12, 2026","place":"Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates","image":"assets/cards/oct12-zeekr-25cm-drift.webp","title":"An SUV Drifts Through a 25-Centimeter Gap","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/33057638","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"UPI reported on October 12 that a Zeekr 7X electric SUV earned a Guinness World Records title after professional driver Chien Jui-Yu passed between two barriers with only 25 centimeters (9.84 inches) of total clearance while drifting at Yas Marina Circuit. The certified attempt itself took place on June 12, 2026, so the publication date and record date are not the same.","why":"A quarter-meter margin split across both sides leaves almost no room for steering error, tire movement or body roll. The record is a controlled precision-driving demonstration on a closed circuit, not evidence that the maneuver is safe on public roads. Naming both clocks also prevents an October report from being mistaken for an October attempt.","angle":"Verified reporting ends above. The Blappos interpretation: Abu Dhabi has invented parallel parking for people who find parallel parking insufficiently hostile. The magnet uses an original generic SUV, invented racetrack scene and fictional markers—no vehicle badge, driver likeness, licensed photograph or suggestion that readers should try it.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"How to Build a Car by Adrian Newey","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/000819680X.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of How to Build a Car by Adrian Newey","quip":"A championship designer's engineering memoir for the part of the stunt that begins long before the tires turn sideways.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/000819680X?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Speed Secrets: Professional Race Driving Techniques","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0760305188.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Speed Secrets by Ross Bentley","quip":"Closed-course technique and car-control theory for understanding precision driving without turning the commute into a record attempt.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0760305188?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"The Physics of NASCAR","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0525950532.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of The Physics of NASCAR by Diandra Leslie-Pelecky","quip":"An accessible tour of grip, weight transfer and racing physics—the forces that make 25 centimeters feel even smaller.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0525950532?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://www.upi.com/Odd_News/2026/10/12/Zeekr-Guinness-World-Records-gap-drift/5951791822673/","sourceName":"Read the October 12 UPI report","sourcePublisher":"UPI","socialSummary":"UPI reported that a Zeekr 7X earned a Guinness record after Chien Jui-Yu drifted through a 25-centimeter total gap at Yas Marina Circuit; the certified attempt occurred June 12 and was reported October 12.","socialPunchline":"Blappos: Parallel parking has entered its boss level."},
{"id":"oct12-1474-pound-fries","isoDate":"2026-10-12","month":"October 2026","date":"Oct 12, 2026","place":"Boise, Idaho","image":"assets/cards/oct12-1474-pound-fries.webp","title":"Idaho Serves a 1,474-Pound Side of Fries","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/33057643","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"UPI reported on October 12 that the Idaho Potato Commission and Spud Daddy set a Guinness World Records mark at Boise Potato Days with 1,474 pounds of fresh-cut french fries. A roughly 50-person crew fed about 1,700 pounds of potatoes through cutters and six commercial fryers before the finished batch was weighed.","why":"The distinction between input weight and finished weight matters: the record was based on cooked fries, not raw potatoes or an estimate. The attempt also turned a familiar side dish into a coordinated production exercise involving food handling, fryer capacity, timing and an official weigh-in.","angle":"Verified reporting ends above. The Blappos interpretation: Idaho has finally answered the restaurant question, “Would you like fries with that?” with a quantity measurable by loading dock. The illustration is an invented fry mountain and generic scale—no event logo, copied photograph, branded carton or claim that one person should eat it.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"The Food Lab: Better Home Cooking Through Science","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0393081087.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of The Food Lab by J. Kenji López-Alt","quip":"The science-heavy kitchen reference for learning why a crisp fry is more than a potato's confident phase.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0393081087?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"The Potato: How the Humble Spud Rescued the Western World","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0865475784.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of The Potato by Larry Zuckerman","quip":"A history of the crop behind the record, before 1,700 pounds of it met six industrial fryers.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0865475784?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"OXO Good Grips 11-Pound Digital Kitchen Food Scale","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/B079D9B82W.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"OXO Good Grips digital kitchen food scale","quip":"A practical home-scale counterpart to the industrial weigh-in—only about 1,463 pounds short of the record.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B079D9B82W?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://www.upi.com/Odd_News/2026/10/12/guinness-food-records-fries-slim-jim/3951791835726/","sourceName":"Read the October 12 UPI report","sourcePublisher":"UPI","socialSummary":"UPI reported that the Idaho Potato Commission and Spud Daddy used about 1,700 pounds of potatoes, six commercial fryers and a 50-person crew to produce a Guinness-record 1,474-pound batch of fresh-cut fries at Boise Potato Days.","socialPunchline":"Blappos: The side order now requires freight classification."},
{"id":"oct12-michigan-7505-km2-flash","isoDate":"2026-10-12","month":"October 2026","date":"Oct 12, 2026","place":"Michigan","image":"assets/cards/oct12-michigan-7505-km2-flash.webp","title":"Michigan Gets a 7,505-Square-Kilometer Flash","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/33057646","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"What Weird Shit Happened Today computed from NOAA GOES Geostationary Lightning Mapper data that a flash with a 7,505-square-kilometer optical footprint was detected at 46.89°N, 88.65°W in Michigan at 9:35 p.m. ET on October 12. The source describes the value as a computed observation from NOAA GOES GLM L2 LCFA data, not an official world record.","why":"The Geostationary Lightning Mapper detects brief optical signals from lightning across wide areas, so an optical footprint is a satellite-derived measurement rather than the path of one cartoon bolt on the ground. Most flashes span roughly 10–100 square kilometers, while megaflashes can exceed 1,000; the 7,505-square-kilometer value is extraordinary but should retain its computed-data label.","angle":"Verified data and its limits end above. The Blappos interpretation: Michigan briefly installed one sky-sized camera flash and forgot to enable red-eye reduction. The magnet uses an original Great Lakes map and invented lightning scene—no NOAA seal, copied satellite frame or claim that the footprint was a ground-strike area.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"All About Lightning","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/048625237X.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of All About Lightning by Martin A. Uman","quip":"A focused science reference for the electrical event beneath the enormous satellite-measured glow.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/048625237X?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"National Geographic Pocket Guide to the Weather of North America","image":"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/P/1426217862.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of National Geographic Pocket Guide to the Weather of North America","quip":"A compact field guide for placing one spectacular Michigan flash inside the continent's larger weather machinery.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1426217862?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Midland ER310 Emergency Crank Weather Radio","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/B015QIC1PW.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Midland ER310 emergency crank weather radio","quip":"The practical storm companion for receiving warnings while the sky is testing its widest flash setting.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B015QIC1PW?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://wwsht.com/2026/10/12/","sourceName":"See the October 12 data digest and NOAA source link","sourcePublisher":"What Weird Shit Happened Today / NOAA","socialSummary":"A WWSHT analysis of NOAA GOES GLM data found a 7,505-square-kilometer optical lightning footprint over Michigan at 9:35 p.m. ET on October 12; it is a computed observation, not an official world record.","socialPunchline":"Blappos: Michigan briefly activated the sky's panorama flash."},
{"id":"oct2-die-another-day","isoDate":"2026-10-02","month":"October 2026","date":"Oct 2, 2026","place":"Nashville, Tennessee","image":"assets/cards/oct2-die-another-day.webp","title":"Die Another Day","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/32651928","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"On September 30, Tennessee attempted to execute death-row prisoner Christa Pike at Riverbend Maximum Security Institution in Nashville using pentobarbital. Officials administered the protocol's initial dose and a second dose, but Pike remained alive. Reuters reported on October 2 that her lawyers said she was unconscious, intubated and on a ventilator in critical condition.","why":"Tennessee's Department of Correction said the written protocol permits no further procedure beyond the steps carried out that night. Governor Bill Lee suspended the state's remaining executions for 2026 and ordered a third-party review. The review had not yet established why the drugs failed to kill Pike, so the medical cause remains unresolved.","angle":"The Blappos angle: Death kept the appointment. Tennessee arrived with a procedure that could not finish the job. A fictional prison administrator searches the manual while an impatient Grim Reaper checks his watch. DIE ANOTHER DAY. The illustration is invented satire of the state process, not a depiction of the execution.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"The Death Penalty: A Reference Handbook","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/1440845492.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"The Death Penalty: A Reference Handbook book cover","quip":"A broad legal and historical reference for a story where the written procedure suddenly matters all the way to its last line.","salesPriority":"primary","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1440845492?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Executioner's Current","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/037572446X.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Executioner's Current book cover","quip":"A history of an earlier American execution technology—and the recurring belief that a new method will make the machinery simple.","salesPriority":"secondary","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/037572446X?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"The Chamber","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/044024594X.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"The Chamber by John Grisham book cover","quip":"A death-row legal thriller for the part of this real story that already reads like a plot twist.","salesPriority":"secondary","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/044024594X?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/tennessee-execution-survivor-christa-pike-ventilator-attorneys-say-2026-10-02/","sourceName":"Read the October 2 Reuters report","sourcePublisher":"Reuters","socialSummary":"Tennessee's failed lethal-injection attempt left Christa Pike unconscious, intubated and on a ventilator, according to her lawyers' October 2 court filing.","socialPunchline":"The state's execution checklist reached the end before the execution did."},
{"id":"oct1-swiss-glaciers","isoDate":"2026-10-01","month":"October","date":"Oct 1, 2026","place":"Swiss Alps","image":"assets/cards/oct1-swiss-glaciers.webp","title":"Swiss glaciers lose more than 5% of their ice in one year","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/32639486","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"Switzerland's glaciers lost more than 5% of their total ice volume during the first eight months of 2026, according to the Swiss glacier-monitoring network cited by Reuters and UPI on October 1. Researchers linked the near-record annual loss to a dry winter, limited snow cover and intense summer heat. The total decline over the past five years is now about one-fifth.","why":"One unusually bad melt season matters because thinner glaciers expose darker ground, reduce their ability to reflect heat and leave less ice to survive the next hot year. The monitoring result is a national aggregate, not a claim that every Swiss glacier lost the same share. The figure also describes physical loss already measured in 2026, not a forecast or a symbolic climate target.","angle":"Verified reporting ends above. The Blappos interpretation: permanent snow has quietly switched to seasonal hours. The magnet turns the monitoring result into an original alpine travel sign with a receding ice line and exposed trail—no copied news photography, institutional logo, named researcher or exact scientific chart.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"Atlas of Vanishing Places","image":"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/P/1781318956.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Atlas of Vanishing Places","quip":"A mapped tour of landscapes under pressure, including the kind of fast-changing ice terrain measured in the Swiss Alps.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1781318956?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"The Melting World: A Journey Across America's Vanishing Glaciers","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/0312546289.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of The Melting World by Christopher White","quip":"A reported journey through glacier science and communities for readers who want the human scale behind percentage losses.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/0312546289?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Field Guide to Alpine Wildlife","image":"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/P/1399409433.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Field Guide to Alpine Wildlife","quip":"A mountain-ecosystem reference for the plants and animals living around the retreating ice line.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1399409433?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://www.reuters.com/sustainability/cop/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-ice-after-record-heatwave-2026-09-30/","sourceName":"Read the October 1 Reuters report"},
{"id":"oct1-guinea-pig","isoDate":"2026-10-01","month":"October","date":"Oct 1, 2026","place":"Grand Junction, Colorado","image":"assets/cards/oct1-guinea-pig.webp","title":"Colorado animal control ends a guinea pig's low-speed getaway","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/32639490","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"Grand Junction Police Department animal-control officers caught a loose guinea pig in a grassy field after approaching it with a towel and coordinating a careful grab. The department shared video of the rescue, and UPI reported it on October 1. The animal was taken to J&M Aquatics & Pet Center and was reported to be doing well; its origin had not been established.","why":"A domestic guinea pig loose outdoors faces traffic, predators, exposure and difficulty finding appropriate food, so the tiny pursuit had a real welfare purpose. The public video supports the capture sequence but not an invented owner, escape route or length of time outside. The safe lesson is to contact local animal control or a rescue rather than turn a frightened small animal into a chase.","angle":"Verified facts end above. The Blappos interpretation: Grand Junction deployed teamwork, patience and one towel to conclude the least aerodynamic pursuit in police history. The card uses an invented field, anonymous officers and a generic guinea pig—not a copied video frame, identifiable employee, pet-center branding or claimed likeness of the rescued animal.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"MidWest Homes for Pets Guinea Habitat Plus","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/B001NJ0DQ8.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"MidWest Homes for Pets Guinea Habitat Plus enclosure","quip":"A roomy, secure habitat aimed directly at preventing the sort of unscheduled field assignment that required a towel team.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B001NJ0DQ8?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Oxbow Essentials Adult Guinea Pig Food","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/B0017JFIDC.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Bag of Oxbow Essentials Adult Guinea Pig Food","quip":"Species-appropriate daily food for the domestic animal whose outdoor menu was neither known nor recommended.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0017JFIDC?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"The Guinea Pig Handbook: Vet-Approved Care for Happy, Healthy Guinea Pigs","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/1438005091.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of The Guinea Pig Handbook","quip":"A care reference for housing, diet and health after the low-speed pursuit ends and responsible ownership begins.","salesPriority":4,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/1438005091?tag=blappos-20"}],"source":"https://www.upi.com/Odd_News/2026/10/01/guinea-pig-grand-junction-colorado/2421790876634/","sourceName":"Read the October 1 UPI report"},
{"id":"oct1-two-headed-turtle","isoDate":"2026-10-01","month":"October","date":"Oct 1, 2026","place":"Cape Cod, Massachusetts","image":"assets/cards/oct1-two-headed-turtle.webp","title":"Cape Cod wildlife center monitors a rare two-headed terrapin","magnetUrl":"https://blappos.printify.me/product/32639492","magnetPrice":"$9.99","facts":"A diamondback terrapin hatchling with two heads is receiving care at Cape Wildlife Center after being found at a protected Wellfleet nesting site and transferred by Mass Audubon. UPI published the case on October 1; the wildlife center had announced the hatchling on September 17. Staff described the condition as bicephaly and said only two comparable cases had reached the center during the previous five years.","why":"Two-headed turtles can face complications with feeding, movement and organ development, so the center is tracking appetite, growth and behavior rather than declaring a prognosis from appearance alone. The report documents one living patient and an unusually careful monitoring plan; it does not establish how long the animal will live or whether both heads control the body equally.","angle":"Verified reporting ends above. The Blappos interpretation: two heads have arrived with one tiny agenda and an entire veterinary clipboard. The magnet uses an original, stylized hatchling and anonymous caregivers—no patient photograph, real person's likeness, institutional mark or claim that the animal is a novelty pet.","amazonLinks":[{"title":"Turtles of the World: A Guide to Every Family","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/069122322X.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg","alt":"Cover of Turtles of the World","quip":"A family-by-family turtle reference that puts one extraordinary diamondback terrapin into its wider biological context.","salesPriority":5,"url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/069122322X?tag=blappos-20"},{"title":"Ecology and Conservation of the Diamond-backed Terrapin","image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/P/1421426269.01.LZZZZZZ